## Review severities (shared with reviewers)

`review-security-code` rates these patterns by this table; the lens's attack-vector law still applies. Change a row here, never in a reviewer.

| Signal | A finding when | Default | Not a finding |
|---|---|---|---|
| Real credential in a committed file (Rule 1) | always | `blocker` | an obvious placeholder or test value |
| Required env var read without startup validation (Rule 1) | always | `minor` | a variable validated elsewhere at startup |
| Query built by interpolation (Rule 2) | external input reaches it | `blocker` with the attack vector stated | a constant or an allowlisted identifier, with the reason read |
| External input reaches the database, filesystem or shell unvalidated (Rule 3) | a named input reaches it | `blocker` with the attack vector stated; `major` if the outcome is wrong but not an attacker's gain | validation already done at the boundary above |
| Credential or secret in a log call (Rule 4) | always | `major` | an identifier or last-four |
| Dependency range `*` / `latest` (Rule 5) | always | `minor` | — |
